A "genuine deref site" is a member read through rStuff -- either
`x->rStuff->member` directly, or `RuleStuff *s = x->rStuff;` followed by
`s->member` with no null test between. The second shape is why the first
grep of this census was VOID: runRuleAction uses it, and a `->rStuff->`
pattern does not match it at all.

